[:db/add "dd0f265d-bfa5-50dc-a4a6-2e74cd7fa586" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "dd0f265d-bfa5-50dc-a4a6-2e74cd7fa586" :answer/value "true"] [:db/ensure "dd0f265d-bfa5-50dc-a4a6-2e74cd7fa586" :answer/validate] [:db/add "ef087a7a-dda5-5c8e-9e5f-dec5cb3d178c" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef087a7a-dda5-5c8e-9e5f-dec5cb3d178c"] [:db/add "ef087a7a-dda5-5c8e-9e5f-dec5cb3d178c" :answer-field/key "Natural numbers ($N$)"] [:db/add "ef087a7a-dda5-5c8e-9e5f-dec5cb3d178c" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/checkbox] [:db/add "ef087a7a-dda5-5c8e-9e5f-dec5cb3d178c" :answer-field/choices "ae63ac59-d057-5432-860e-d0e4844a340c"] [:db/add "ef087a7a-dda5-5c8e-9e5f-dec5cb3d178c" :answer-field/choices "dd0f265d-bfa5-50dc-a4a6-2e74cd7fa586"] [:db/add "ef087a7a-dda5-5c8e-9e5f-dec5cb3d178c" :answer-field/correct "ae63ac59-d057-5432-860e-d0e4844a340c"] [:db/ensure "ef087a7a-dda5-5c8e-9e5f-dec5cb3d178c" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16" :question/id #uuid "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16"] [:db/add "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $\\sqrt{58}$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/add "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16" :question/worked-solution "![](images/67/67ef97be4b21a74feaae15f3ff30d5077fc1316874df8de79155316a621e4487.png)\n\nRecall the following:\n\n- $N$ represents the set of **natural numbers**.\n\n- $Z$ represents the set of **integers**.\n\n- $Q$ represents the set of **rational numbers**.\n\n- $R$ represents the set of **real numbers**.\n\n- $C$ represents the set of **complex numbers**.\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The number $\\sqrt{58}$ is not an integer, so it does *not* belong to $Z$ nor to $N.$ We can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{58}\\notin N\\qquad \\sqrt{58}\\notin Z\n$$\n\n- Also, $\\sqrt{58}$ is irrational because $58$ is positive and not a perfect square. It cannot be written as the ratio of two integers, so it does *not* belong to $Q$ either:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{58}\\notin Q\n$$\n\n- Every irrational number is both a real number and a complex number. Consequently, $\\sqrt{58}$ belongs to both $R$ and $C,$ and we can write\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{58}\\in R\\qquad \\sqrt{58}\\in C\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $R, C$ only."] [:db/add "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16" :question/answer-fields "4f95145a-790e-54d9-82af-5f6f8dc5caf5"] [:db/add "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16" :question/answer-fields "7c4d8949-38b7-55b8-8816-5e917c526d14"] [:db/add "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16" :question/answer-fields "9ed617ef-0ff0-5d0f-84f6-30736d30f211"] [:db/add "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16" :question/answer-fields "972578a5-a401-5229-b3e0-e0e7f1ab6a23"] [:db/add "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16" :question/answer-fields "ef087a7a-dda5-5c8e-9e5f-dec5cb3d178c"] [:db/ensure "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186054814 :knowledge-point/questions "db5a74cd-1494-5d20-90cc-b56ee7af9d16"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "959b44ac-2395-5cbd-864d-61762dc91afa"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/script "generators/70/70f4dd39b0e2facb701fbc919240d73c573f2493485f252ad27834a0bcccbf12/generator.py"] [:db/add 17592186054814 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] [:db/ensure 17592186054814 :knowledge-point/validate]]
